Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: So lahat ng concern ninyo ay aming inaaral sa ginagawa namin budget ng 2027 na budget.

2166
01:32:15,940 --> 01:32:24,200
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: At napapasalamat kami sa inyo na ito ay ginagawa ninyong advocacy na kami sa appropriation.

2167
01:32:24,860 --> 01:32:32,180
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Nakakaroon kami ng guide mula sa inyo na maaaring makatulong sa amin doon sa paggawa namin ng tamang budget sa 2027.

2168
01:32:32,500 --> 01:32:41,400
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Rest assured, lahat ng inyong sinasabi sa amin ay aming itong siseryosohin para may pagpapasa namin ng budget natin ngayong 2027.

2169
01:32:42,040 --> 01:32:45,680
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Ay kaugnay namin kayo, may participation kayo.

2170
01:32:45,680 --> 01:33:00,940
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: At sa ginagawa namin ito, natitiyakin namin, siyempre sa utos ng ating Pangulo, na yung pagiging sensitive namin sa ginagawa namin budget ng ating bansa ay nararapat na ayon at kailangan ng ating mga kababayan.

2171
01:33:01,600 --> 01:33:11,420
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Hindi lamang ito dahil sa figure, kung hindi ito ay dapat malaman namin yung totoong hinayin ng ating bansa at yun yung dapat namin gawin sa appropriation namin dito sa Kongreso.

2172
01:33:11,720 --> 01:33:15,140
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: So muli po, maraming maraming salamat po sa inyong lahat.

2173
01:33:15,140 --> 01:33:22,340
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: At ito pong lahat ng ito ay amin pong dadalhin sa committee para po aming upuan at nalagyan po namin ng tamang sagot ang inyong katanungan.

2174
01:33:22,980 --> 01:33:23,560
Rep. Reynante U. Arrogancia: Salamat po ulit.

2175
01:33:24,260 --> 01:33:26,420
John Castillo: Thank you very much, Vice Chair Reynan.

2176
01:33:27,580 --> 01:33:30,980
John Castillo: Any other feedbacks from our panelists, SVC?

2177
01:33:31,520 --> 01:33:38,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Yes, maraming salamat, Vice Chair Reynan, for your answers to address some of the concerns.

2178
01:33:38,740 --> 01:33:43,740
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: I would like to commend Miss Fajardo.

2179
01:33:45,140 --> 01:34:09,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Isabel, for your comments and suggestions talagang with this engagement and all the other NGOs ang dami namin natututunan that these informations we can really use to amend or modify some of the budget of the departments to address the concerns.

2180
01:34:09,860 --> 01:34:14,340
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So perspective matters and you're giving us new perspective.

2181
01:34:15,140 --> 01:34:19,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: That we can use in order to improve our budgets further.

2182
01:34:19,900 --> 01:34:26,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kanina habang nakikinig kay Miss Fajardo, parang dinidescribe nyo na po yung meritocracy.

2183
01:34:26,800 --> 01:34:45,020
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kasi from spending or process-based budgeting, kung saan ginegrade ngayon for efficiency of spending or not spending, yung meritocracy, same as what you said, kailangan outcome-based din.

2184
01:34:45,140 --> 01:34:49,620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So dahil mas makikita natin yung impact.

2185
01:34:49,620 --> 01:35:02,380
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So unlike now na talagang is everything above board, sumunod ba sa process, but aside from that, did it make an impact dun sa buhay ng ating mga mamamayan?

2186
01:35:02,540 --> 01:35:11,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And that is the essence of the meritocracy bill na hindi lang process-based but also outcome-based.

2187
01:35:11,320 --> 01:35:12,140
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So.

2188
01:35:13,260 --> 01:35:14,420
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So.

2189
01:35:15,140 --> 01:35:18,000
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: You hit the nail right on the head.

2190
01:35:18,760 --> 01:35:24,160
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And since mobility yung pinag-uusapan natin, ito yung isang advocacy po ng inyong lingkod.

2191
01:35:24,160 --> 01:35:27,300
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And hardly anyone is talking about it.

2192
01:35:27,960 --> 01:35:44,020
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Is that, do we know that we're losing 3.5 billion pesos a day because of the inefficiencies ng ating infrastructure, ng ating ekonomiya?

2193
01:35:44,020 --> 01:35:45,120
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Tanghali na po.

2194
01:35:45,140 --> 01:35:52,600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Ngayon, mamaya hapo na, and we lost 3.5 billion pesos a day, another 3.5 billion pesos.

2195
01:35:53,360 --> 01:36:06,380
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And if you compute that in one year, yan na po yung capital outlay ng ating current budget, amounting to 1.2, 1.3 trillion pesos.

2196
01:36:06,380 --> 01:36:14,500
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So yan na halos yung pinagdibatihan ngayon sa House and eventually with the Senate, sa BICAM.

2197
01:36:15,140 --> 01:36:34,720
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Na 1.2 to 1.3 trillion na katulad nung sinabi, ito na lang yung leeway natin dahil yung iba, naka-earmark na po or pang sweldo na or MOE na hindi na natin masyadong pwedeng mamodify.

2198
01:36:34,720 --> 01:36:34,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Okay.

2199
01:36:35,440 --> 01:36:35,580
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So.

2200
01:36:37,160 --> 01:36:39,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Na ano lang po siya.

2201
01:36:39,760 --> 01:36:40,120
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Kumbaga.

2202
01:36:41,840 --> 01:36:44,960
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Na offset lang po siya nitong losses.

2203
01:36:44,960 --> 01:36:46,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: 3.5 billion pesos a day.

2204
01:36:47,760 --> 01:36:54,280
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And kinumpute ko po ito from when the study started, JICA study po ito.

2205
01:36:54,780 --> 01:36:58,380
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Simula 2014, 2.5 billion pesos a day pa lang.

2206
01:36:58,860 --> 01:37:01,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: In update ng 2017, 3.5 na.

2207
01:37:02,480 --> 01:37:12,600
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And according to the same study, kung hindi ma-solusyonan, by 2030, aakyat ng 5.4 billion pesos a day.

2208
01:37:13,080 --> 01:37:14,620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, anlaki po nun.

2209
01:37:14,620 --> 01:37:24,860
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: And to date, kinumpute ko po, kung accurate yung study, we've lost 13.7 trillion pesos already.

2210
01:37:25,760 --> 01:37:27,180
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Twice the current budget.

2211
01:37:28,360 --> 01:37:43,800
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, ito po, kung nagtataka po yung ating mga kasama, ito po because of the inefficiencies ng congestion, time wasted, pollution, work-life balance compromised, productivity loss, opportunity loss, and so on and so forth.

2212
01:37:43,800 --> 01:38:03,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, napakalaking problema po nito, ito yung sinasabi ko na hinahabol natin yung mga allegedly corrupt, yun yung sins of commission, pero hindi natin napapansin yung sins of omission.

2213
01:38:03,560 --> 01:38:13,260
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Which is, in this case, a lot bigger than any man-made or natural disaster that hit us.

2214
01:38:13,640 --> 01:38:13,780
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, it's a big problem.

2215
01:38:13,780 --> 01:38:18,520
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, dun po ang isang magiging relevance nung meritocracy bill.

2216
01:38:18,700 --> 01:38:22,540
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: It will address that and incentivize good performance

2217
01:38:22,540 --> 01:38:26,240
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: para proactively mabawasan yung sense of commission

2218
01:38:26,240 --> 01:38:31,320
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: at proactively ma-incentivize yung performance.

2219
01:38:32,440 --> 01:38:36,100
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: So, I just wanted to bring that up

2220
01:38:36,100 --> 01:38:38,620
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: and rest assured lahat po nung binanggit ninyo,

2221
01:38:38,720 --> 01:38:39,560
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: naka-record po yan,

2222
01:38:40,200 --> 01:38:42,660
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: at nandito po yung ating vice chair

2223
01:38:42,660 --> 01:38:47,340
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: at malalaman nyo rin po kung ano yung mga changes

2224
01:38:47,340 --> 01:38:50,780
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: that we will recommend to address all those concerns.

2225
01:38:51,200 --> 01:38:51,700
Rep. Albert S. Garcia: Salamat po.

